## Good example

### A date picker that can be dismissed using a keyboard

A user tabs to a date picker in a form and presses Tab to move into the widget. They use the arrow keys to choose a date and press Tab again before selecting 'Done'. This moves them to the next form field.

This widget would pass because the user was able to move into, around, and exit the date picker and continue with their user journey. Additionally, it aligns with what controls the user expects, such as being able to tab to the Done button and press it, or use Esc to leave.

